    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d455">

                <pb facs="0860" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg764"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862i.73/41</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Netherlands Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >De Beaufort</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 540</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have not failed to communicate to my
                    Government the text of the memorandum containing a tentative draft of an
                    arrangement <pb facs="0861" n="765" xml:id="pg765"/> between the Five Powers
                    regarding the disposal of the Yap Cables formerly owned by the Netherland German
                    Telegraph Company which memorandum was handed to me by the State Department in
                    January last.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d455-f1"/></p>
                <p>Referring to paragraph three of this memorandum and acting upon instructions
                    received from my Government, I have now the honor to inform the United States
                    Government that the Netherland Government accepts the Yap–Menado Cable under the
                    arrangement as set forth in the memorandum, copy of which is enclosed
                    herewith.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. de Beaufort</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d455-f1" n="10" xml:id="d455-f1-content">
                <p>Memorandum not printed; it consisted of the text of the draft of arrangement
                    quoted in the Under Secretary’s memorandum of Mar. 25, 1922, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
